      "title": "Director of Residence Life and Community Standards",
      "description": "Director of Residence Life and Community Standards - HigherEdJobs Skip to main content Hide this notification New job search filters and job description pages are here. We'd love your feedback! Share Feedback Sign Up | Log In Log In Sign Up Job Search By Category Administrative Faculty Executive By Location Metro/Region State/Province Country Remote By School Four-Year Institutions Two-Year Institutions All Institutions Institutional Profiles By Type Dual Career Today's Jobs Adjunct/Part-Time Inclusive Workplace Military-Friendly Advanced Search My Account Signed out Account Home Job Alerts Resume/CV Other Documents My Jobs Organizer Profile Account Settings News & Resources News Advice & News Higher Ed Careers Author in Residence Ask the Expert Newsletters HigherEdJobs Podcast Resources Career Resources Job Search Tips Resume/CV Writing Service Workplace Inclusion Search Firms Employers Home Login Create Account Job Postings Post a Single Job Job Packs Unlimited Postings VIP Positions Automated Postings Other Products Digital Advertising Resume Database Institutional Profile Interim Search View All Products Posting Upgrades Inclusive Workplace Upgrade Inclusive Workplace Spotlight Priority Job Upgrade Military Upgrade Social Media Upgrade Featured Executive Position More Info Our Audience Testimonials Pay Your Invoice Contact Us Home Jobs Institution Job Listings Job Detail CU Director of Residence Life and Community Standards Centenary University Hackettstown, NJ $70,000 - $85,000 per year Apply Now Share this position Copy link Email LinkedIn Facebook X (Twitter) Salary $70,000 - $85,000 per year Job Type Full-Time Category Residence Life and Housing ; Student Affairs and Services Posted 1 day ago (Reposted Job: Initially posted on 09/09/2026) Apply By Dec 6, 2026 16 days left Website www.centenaryuniversity.edu About Centenary University Centenary University launches students into a successful career and life. Guided by our strategic priorities of Student Success, University Vitality, and World Engagement, we are committed to creating a campus environment where students thrive academically, personally, and professionally. Position Summary Centenary University seeks a collaborative, student-centered leader to serve as Director of Residence Life and Community Standards. This position provides strategic leadership for all aspects of residential life, housing operations, community standards, residential education, student engagement, and leadership development. The Director is responsible for creating and sustaining residential communities that are safe, respectful, inclusive, engaging, and supportive of student success. The Director oversees housing operations, occupancy management, residential education initiatives, student conduct processes, crisis response, staff development, and community-building efforts that foster belonging and personal growth. This position works closely with Facilities, Campus Safety, Counseling Services, Health Services, Information Technology, Enrollment Management, Athletics, Academic Affairs, and other campus partners to deliver an outstanding residential experience. This position does not require residence in university housing. The Director is expected to participate in an administrative on-call rotation and provide leadership during emergencies and critical incidents as needed. Key Responsibilities Residential Life & Housing Operations Lead all aspects of housing operations, occupancy management, room assignments, openings and closings, and housing communications. Manage residential occupancy forecasting and housing utilization strategies. Oversee housing systems, policies, and operational processes. Partner with Enrollment, Athletics, Financial Services, and Student Affairs to support student recruitment and retention goals. Community Standards & Student Conduct Administer the student conduct process and residential policies. Ensure conduct cases are addressed fairly, consistently, and educationally. Facilitate conflict resolution and restorative practices. Analyze conduct trends and implement proactive educational interventions. Student Engagement & Leadership Development Develop a comprehensive residential engagement strategy supporting belonging, leadership, and retention. Support student leadership councils, advisory groups, and residential programming initiatives. Create opportunities for students to engage, lead, serve, and contribute to community life. Collaborate with campus partners to strengthen the student experience. Staff Leadership Recruit, train, supervise, develop, and evaluate professional and student staff. Foster a culture of accountability, engagement, service, and student support. Provide ongoing coaching and professional development opportunities. Crisis Response & Student Support Lead residential crisis response and emergency management efforts. Maintain effective on-call systems and emergency protocols. Coordinate with Campus Safety, Counseling Services, and Health Services to support students during critical incidents. Facilities & Strategic Planning Collaborate with Facilities on maintenance, renovations, and capital improvement projects. Conduct facility inspections and advocate for improvements that enhance student safety and experience. Lead assessment, planning, and continuous improvement initiatives to strengthen student outcomes and residential occupancy. Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Higher Education, Student Affairs, Counseling, Leadership, Education, or a related field. Five or more years of progressively responsible experience in Residence Life, Housing, Student Affairs, Student Conduct, or a comparable leadership role. Demonstrated experience supervising professional and student staff. Experience administering student conduct processes, conflict resolution, and crisis response. Strong leadership, communication, organizational, and relationship-building skills. Ability to work occasional evenings and weekends in support of residential operations, student programs, opening and closing periods, and emergency situations. Ability to participate in an administrative on-call rotation and respond effectively to emergencies and critical incidents. Why Join Centenary? This is an opportunity to shape the residential experience for students, build vibrant communities, and directly contribute to student engagement, belonging, retention, and success. The Director will play a key leadership role in fostering communities where students feel connected, supported, and empowered to thrive. Centenary University is a learning community comprised of multifaceted and complex differences and we welcome all. We offer a supportive environment that promotes acceptance, a culture of service, skills of critical thought, and purposeful action. We are responsible for the efforts needed to create the change we seek. Equal Employment Opportunity has been, and will continue to be, a fundamental principle at Centenary University where employment is based upon personal capabilities and qualifications without discrimination because of race, color, religion, sex, age, national or ethnic origin, sexual orientation, marital status, service in Armed Forces, disability or any other protected characteristic as established by law. This policy of Equal Employment Opportunity applies to policies and procedures relating to recruitment, hiring, promotion, compensation, benefits, termination and other terms and conditions of employment. Apply Now Share this position Copy link Email LinkedIn Facebook X (Twitter) CU Centenary University 4-Year & Advanced · Hackettstown, NJ At the main campus in Hackettstown, N.J., the equestrian center, and the Parsippany campus, the University enrolls approximately 1,100 undergraduate students and a nearly equal number of adult and graduate... 3 open positions View profile Create your free job search account Edit and manage Job Alerts Post your resume/CV Tr