      "title": "Student Success Administrator",
      "description": "Student Success Administrator - HigherEdJobs Your Privacy We use cookies and other similar technologies to enhance user experience, for website maintenance purposes, and to analyze performance and traffic on our website. We also share information about your use of our website with advertising and analytics partners. If we have detected an opt-out preference signal, then it will be honored. Further information is available in our Privacy Policy . Do Not Sell My Personal Information I understand Skip to main content Hide this notification New job search filters and job description pages are here. We'd love your feedback! Share Feedback Sign Up | Log In Log In Sign Up Job Search By Category Administrative Faculty Executive By Location Metro/Region State/Province Country Remote By School Four-Year Institutions Two-Year Institutions All Institutions Institutional Profiles By Type Dual Career Today's Jobs Adjunct/Part-Time Inclusive Workplace Military-Friendly Advanced Search My Account Signed out Account Home Job Alerts Resume/CV Other Documents My Jobs Organizer Profile Account Settings News & Resources News Advice & News Higher Ed Careers Author in Residence Ask the Expert Newsletters HigherEdJobs Podcast Resources Career Resources Job Search Tips Resume/CV Writing Service Workplace Inclusion Search Firms Employers Home Login Create Account Job Postings Post a Single Job Job Packs Unlimited Postings VIP Positions Automated Postings Other Products Digital Advertising Resume Database Institutional Profile Interim Search View All Products Posting Upgrades Inclusive Workplace Upgrade Inclusive Workplace Spotlight Priority Job Upgrade Military Upgrade Social Media Upgrade Featured Executive Position More Info Our Audience Testimonials Pay Your Invoice Contact Us Home Jobs Institution Job Listings Job Detail CU Student Success Administrator Centenary University Hackettstown, NJ $45,000 - $60,000 per year Apply Now Share this position Copy link Email LinkedIn Facebook X (Twitter) Salary $45,000 - $60,000 per year Job Type Full-Time Category Student Affairs and Services ; Academic Advising Posted 3 days ago Website www.centenaryuniversity.edu Centenary University Mission & Priorities Centenary University launches students into a successful career and life. Centenary advances three strategic priorities: Student Success, University Vitality, and World Engagement. Position Summary The Student Success Administrator serves as a key member of the Student Success team, providing proactive outreach, student support coordination, case management, student advocacy, and administrative leadership for student success initiatives. The Student Success Administrator works with students from a holistic perspective, recognizing that academic achievement, personal wellbeing, financial stability, and campus engagement are interconnected contributors to student success. This position serves as a primary point of contact for students seeking assistance and collaborates closely with campus partners including Financial Aid, the Registrar's Office, Academic Affairs, Accessibility Services, Residence Life, Student Life, Wellness Services, Athletics, and faculty to identify and remove barriers to persistence. Through coordinated interventions, follow-up support, and data-informed outreach, the Student Success Administrator contributes directly to student retention, academic progress, and graduation goals. Core Responsibilities and Expected Outcomes 1. Student Outreach and Early Intervention Monitor alerts, referrals, academic progress indicators, attendance concerns, and other student success data. Conduct proactive outreach to students experiencing academic, personal, financial, or engagement-related challenges. Facilitate follow-up and document intervention efforts. Outcome: Students receive timely support and intervention before concerns escalate, improving persistence and academic success. 2. Student Success Coordination Coordinate the intake, assignment, and tracking of student success cases referred through faculty, staff, self-referral, early alert systems, and other university processes. Conduct initial intake meetings, gather and document relevant information, maintain accurate case records, monitor case progression, and ensure timely follow-up and coordination with campus partners. Maintain oversight of student success documentation, record-keeping practices, and case management systems to support effective service delivery and reporting. Outcome: Student success cases are processed efficiently, records remain accurate and compliant, students are connected to appropriate resources in a timely manner, and case management data supports effective intervention, collaboration, and retention efforts. 3. Holistic Student Support and Resource Navigation Support students with concerns related to academic performance, wellness, financial challenges, campus engagement, time management, goal setting, and adjustment to university life. Utilize a strengths-based and student-centered approach to help students identify barriers, develop action plans, and connect with appropriate resources. Outcome: Students experience seamless access to campus resources, develop greater self-advocacy skills, and build stronger connections to the University community. 4. Retention and Persistence Initiatives Assist with the implementation of retention campaigns, student success programming, re-enrollment efforts, academic recovery initiatives, and persistence strategies. Coordinate communications and outreach related to student success milestones. Outcome: Retention and persistence efforts are executed effectively and contribute to improved student outcomes. 5. Student Records, Data Management, and Reporting Maintain accurate student records, case notes, referrals, and intervention documentation within university systems. Generate reports related to outreach efforts, retention initiatives, and student success outcomes. Outcome: Student success data is accurate, accessible, and supports informed decision-making. 6. Administrative and Operational Support Provide administrative support for the Student Success Center, including scheduling, correspondence, meeting coordination, purchasing, record maintenance, and office operations. Outcome: Student Success operations are efficient, organized, and responsive to student needs. 7. Assessment, Continuous Improvement, and Compliance Support assessment efforts related to student success initiatives and retention programs. Maintain compliance with FERPA and university policies while identifying opportunities to improve services and student outcomes. Outcome: Services remain compliant, data-informed, and aligned with university goals for student success and retention. 8. Student Success Center Environment and Student Experience Create and maintain a welcoming, engaging, and student-centered environment within the Student Success Center. Coordinate office appearance, seasonal and thematic decorations, student-focused displays, resource materials, and promotional messaging that foster belonging, connection, and engagement. Develop creative approaches to recognize student achievements, celebrate milestones, and promote student success initiatives. Coordinate small-scale engagement activities, resource awareness campaigns, welcome initiatives, and student success events that encourage student participation and utilization of campus resources. Ensure the center serves as a warm and inviting space where students feel comfortable seeking support and building connections. Outcome: Students experience a welcoming and supportive environment that encourages engagement with Student Success services, strengthens their sense of belonging, and promotes connection to the Centenary community. All Other Duties as Assigned Qualifications Required Bachelor's degree or equivalent combination of education and relevant experience. Two or more years of experience in higher education, student services, advising, case management, customer service, administrative support, or a related field. Strong interpersonal, communication, and relationship-building skills. Demonstrated commitment to supporting diverse student populations. Excellent organizational skills and ability to manage multiple priorities. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite, including Outlook, Word, Excel, and Teams. Ability to maintain confidential information and comply with FERPA requirements. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with students, faculty, and staff. Preferred Experience in student success, academic advising, retention, persistence, student affairs, or higher education administration. Experience providing support to students navigating academic, personal, financial, or wellbeing-related concerns. Experience using student information systems, CRM platforms, and early-alert technologies such as Pharos360. Knowledge of retention strategies, student development theory, and student support practices. Experience interpreting student success data and preparing reports. Familiarity with higher education policies, academic processes, and student support resources. Demonstrated ability to exercise sound judgment, maintain confidentiality, and manage sensitive student situations. Competencies Student-Centered Service Case Management and Follow-Through Communication and Relationship Building Collaboration and Teamwork Problem Solving and Resource Navigation Organization and Attention to Detail Cultural Awareness and Inclusion Data Management and Reporting Professional Judgment and Discretion Commitment to Student Success and Retention Physical Requirements and Work Environment Primarily office-based work environment. Frequent interaction with students, faculty, staff, and families. Ability to move throughout campus to attend meetings, events, and student appointments. Ability to operate standard office equipment and technology. Occasional evening or weekend hours may be required to support orientation programs, retention initiatives, student success events, and other university activities. Centenary Values - Centenary RISE Curiosity • Respect • Innovation • Service • Excellence Through Centenary RISE, the Student Success team advances a culture where academic achievement, wellbeing, belonging, and personal growth work together to promote student persistence, graduation, and lifelong success. The Student Success Administrator contributes to these efforts by helping students access resources, navigate challenges, build resilience, and develop meaningful connections to the Centenary community. Centenary University is a learning community comprised of multifaceted and complex differences and we welcome all. We offer a supportive environment that promotes acceptance, a culture of service, skills of critical thought, and purposeful action. We are responsible for the efforts needed to create the change we seek. Equal Employment Opportunity has been, and will continue to be, a fundamental principle at Centenary University where employment is based upon personal capabilities and qualifications without discrimination because of race, color, religion, sex, age, national or ethnic origin, sexual orientation, marital status, service in Armed Forces, disability or any other protected characteristic as established by law. This policy of Equal Employment Opportunity applies to policies and procedures relating to recruitment, hiring, promotion, compensation, benefits, termination and other terms and conditions of employment. Apply Now Share this position Copy link Email LinkedIn Facebook X (Twitter) CU Centenary University 4-Year & Advanced · Hackettstown, NJ At the main campus in Hackettstown, N.J., the equestrian center, and the Parsippany campus, the University enrolls approximately 1,100 undergraduate students and a nearly equal number of adult and graduate... 3 open positions View profile Create your free job search account Edit and manage Job Alerts Post your resume/CV Track your applications Join Now Have an account? Sign in To Apply for this Job Email: sasha.jackson@centenaryuniversity.edu OR Apply through HigherEdJobs Please be sure to read the job posting carefully and submit all required information. Job Seekers Search Jobs Job Seeker Login Advice & News Newsletter Sign-Up Employers Post A Job All Recruitment Products Employer Login Testimonials Company About Us Contact Us Advertise with Us Our Audience Job Seekers Search Jobs Job Seeker Login Advice & News Newsletter Sign-Up Employers Post A Job All Recruitment Products Employer Login Testimonials Company About Us Contact Us Advertise with Us Our Audience Privacy Policy | Terms of Use | Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information © 2026 HigherEdJobs. U.S. Patent 8,548,928 Email this job to a friend Email Job To Please enter a single email address Your Email Your Name Message Insider Update Sign me up for the Insider Update , HigherEdJobs' newsletter for career-focused higher education professionals. Privacy Policy Insider Career Track: -- Select a Career Track -- Student Faculty Member (Tenured) Faculty Member (Non-Tenured) Post Doctorate Adjunct/Part-Time Administrative/Staff Executive (Director, Asst/Assoc VP/Dean) Senior Executive (VP, Dean, President/Chancellor) Please type the characters to the left above (case sensitive). Close Job Seeker Login Email Password Keep me signed in Log In Forgot your password? Don't have an account? Sign Up (New) Terms and Conditions of Use (Updated) Privacy Policy"
