      "title": "Non-clinical Case Manager",
      "description": "Non-clinical Case Manager - HigherEdJobs Skip to main content Hide this notification New job search filters and job description pages are here. We'd love your feedback! Share Feedback Sign Up | Log In Log In Sign Up Job Search By Category Administrative Faculty Executive By Location Metro/Region State/Province Country Remote By School Four-Year Institutions Two-Year Institutions All Institutions Institutional Profiles By Type Dual Career Today's Jobs Adjunct/Part-Time Inclusive Workplace Military-Friendly Advanced Search My Account Signed out Account Home Job Alerts Resume/CV Other Documents My Jobs Organizer Profile Account Settings News & Resources News Advice & News Higher Ed Careers Author in Residence Ask the Expert Newsletters HigherEdJobs Podcast Resources Career Resources Job Search Tips Resume/CV Writing Service Workplace Inclusion Search Firms Employers Home Login Create Account Job Postings Post a Single Job Job Packs Unlimited Postings VIP Positions Automated Postings Other Products Digital Advertising Resume Database Institutional Profile Interim Search View All Products Posting Upgrades Inclusive Workplace Upgrade Inclusive Workplace Spotlight Priority Job Upgrade Military Upgrade Social Media Upgrade Featured Executive Position More Info Our Audience Testimonials Pay Your Invoice Contact Us Home Jobs Institution Job Listings Job Detail CU Non-clinical Case Manager Centenary University Hackettstown, NJ $25 per hour Apply Now Share this position Copy link Email LinkedIn Facebook X (Twitter) Salary $25 per hour Job Type Full-Time Category Student Affairs and Services Posted Today Apply By Dec 14, 2026 20 days left Website www.centenaryuniversity.edu Centenary University Mission & Priorities Centenary University launches students into a successful career and life. Centenary advances three strategic priorities: Student Success, University Vitality, and World Engagement Position Summary The Non-Clinical Case Manager is a 10-month position providing individualized case management and coordinated support to students experiencing challenges that may affect their well-being, academic progress, safety, or continued enrollment. The position assists students in identifying needs, accessing campus and community resources, navigating University processes, and connecting with appropriate support services. Working collaboratively with the Care Team, Student Affairs, academic departments, and external service providers, the Case Manager helps facilitate timely referrals, consistent follow-up, and continuity of support for students with complex or ongoing needs. The position supports student success and retention through a non-clinical, student-centered approach that promotes access to resources, self-advocacy, and connection to the University community. Core Responsibilities and Expected Outcomes Student Case Management & Support Responsibilities Manage a caseload of students requiring additional support, intervention, or resource coordination. Conduct needs assessments, develop individualized support plans, and coordinate appropriate referrals and follow-up services. Assist students in navigating academic, financial, housing, wellness, personal, and basic-needs challenges. Provide non-clinical case management while connecting students with licensed professionals and specialized services when appropriate. Expected Outcomes Students receive timely, coordinated, and individualized support. Barriers to student success are addressed through effective intervention, resource connection, and follow-up. Students demonstrate increased utilization of support services and progress toward identified goals. Care Team Coordination & Student Intervention Responsibilities Partner with the Care Team and campus stakeholders to identify, assess, monitor, and support students of concern. Coordinate referrals, intervention plans, follow-up activities, and case communication in accordance with university policies and privacy requirements. Support the continuous improvement of Care Team processes, protocols, and tracking systems. Expected Outcomes Students of concern receive coordinated and timely interventions. Follow-up activities and referrals are completed consistently and effectively. Campus collaboration supports continuity of care and student success. Resource Navigation & Basic Needs Support Responsibilities Connect students with campus and community resources, including food, housing, financial assistance, healthcare, transportation, and social services. Assist students in understanding eligibility requirements, navigating referral processes, and accessing available benefits and support programs. Maintain relationships with community agencies and oversee programs supporting basic-needs security, including the Cyclone Food Pantry and Cyclone Thrift Shop. Expected Outcomes Students successfully access needed resources and services. Barriers to meeting basic needs are reduced. Community partnerships strengthen the University's support network. Campus Collaboration & Continuity of Care Responsibilities Consult and collaborate with faculty, staff, families, campus departments, and external partners to coordinate support for students experiencing challenges. Support students transitioning back to campus following hospitalization, treatment, or other significant life events. Facilitate coordinated communication, service delivery, and referrals across the University. Expected Outcomes Students experience seamless support across campus services. Transition and follow-up plans promote continuity of care and student well-being. Campus partners have a clear process for consultation, referral, and coordinated support. Assessment, Documentation & Reporting Responsibilities Maintain accurate and confidential case records using approved case-management systems. Monitor key indicators including referral outcomes, service utilization, student needs, and intervention effectiveness. Prepare reports and recommendations that support assessment, planning, and continuous improvement. Expected Outcomes Case documentation is accurate, timely, and compliant with university requirements. Data informs decision-making, resource allocation, and service enhancements. Trends and service gaps are identified and addressed proactively. Outreach, Education & Student Resource Awareness Responsibilities Promote awareness of student support services and available resources through outreach, education, and consultation. Assist students, faculty, and staff in understanding referral pathways and accessing support services. Support university initiatives that encourage help-seeking behaviors and early intervention. Expected Outcomes Students demonstrate increased awareness and utilization of support resources. Faculty and staff effectively identify and refer students in need. Early intervention contributes to improved student well-being, persistence, and success. Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Social Work, Psychology, Criminal Justice, Human Services, or a related field. Demonstrated ability to assess needs, coordinate resources and referrals, and provide effective support to individuals experiencing complex or sensitive circumstances. Strong communication, interpersonal, organizational, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and cases effectively. Ability to exercise sound judgment, maintain confidentiality, establish appropriate professional boundaries, and recognize when concerns require escalation or referral. Demonstrated ability to collaborate effectively with students, faculty, staff, administrators, community agencies, and external service providers. Commitment to student success, well-being, and a student-centered approach to support and service delivery. Preferred Qualifications Experience in case management, student support services, social services, higher education, behavioral health, or a related field. Knowledge of community resources, public benefits, and support services related to basic needs, wellness, and student success. Experience working with students experiencing academic, financial, housing, personal, or wellness-related challenges. Familiarity with FERPA, case management systems, and best practices in student support and intervention. Reporting Structure Reports to: Vice President for Student Affairs. Compensation and Funding This is a full-time position partially grant supported an hourly rate of 25.00. Employment Conditions This position requires occasional evening or weekend responsibilities to support student outreach, campus events, and urgent student support needs. Additional duties may be assigned in support of student success and university priorities. The University reserves the right to modify the position's duties and responsibilities based on institutional needs, applicable policies, and available funding. Centenary University is a learning community comprised of multifaceted and complex differences and we welcome all. We offer a supportive environment that promotes acceptance, a culture of service, skills of critical thought, and purposeful action. We are responsible for the efforts needed to create the change we seek. Equal Employment Opportunity has been, and will continue to be, a fundamental principle at Centenary University where employment is based upon personal capabilities and qualifications without discrimination because of race, color, religion, sex, age, national or ethnic origin, sexual orientation, marital status, service in Armed Forces, disability or any other protected characteristic as established by law. This policy of Equal Employment Opportunity applies to policies and procedures relating to recruitment, hiring, promotion, compensation, benefits, termination and other terms and conditions of employment. Apply Now Share this position Copy link Email LinkedIn Facebook X (Twitter) CU Centenary University 4-Year & Advanced · Hackettstown, NJ At the main campus in Hackettstown, N.J., the equestrian center, and the Parsippany campus, the University enrolls approximately 1,100 undergraduate students and a nearly equal number of adult and graduate... 5 open positions View profile Create your free job search account Edit and manage Job Alerts Post your resume/CV Track your applications Join Now Have an account? Sign in To Apply for this Job Email: Kerry.mullins@centenaryuniversity.edu OR Apply through HigherEdJobs Please be sure to read the job posting carefully and submit all required information. Job Seekers Search Jobs Job Seeker Login Advice & News Newsletter Sign-Up Employers Post A Job All Recruitment Products Employer Login Testimonials Company About Us Contact Us Advertise with Us Our Audience Job Seekers Search Jobs Job Seeker Login Advice & News Newsletter Sign-Up Employers Post A Job All Recruitment Products Employer Login Testimonials Company About Us Contact Us Advertise with Us Our Audience Privacy Policy | Terms of Use | Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information © 2026 HigherEdJobs. U.S. Patent 8,548,928 Email this job to a friend Email Job To Please enter a single email address Your Email Your Name Message Insider Update Sign me up for the Insider Update , HigherEdJobs' newsletter for career-focused higher education professionals. Privacy Policy Insider Career Track: -- Select a Career Track -- Student Faculty Member (Tenured) Faculty Member (Non-Tenured) Post Doctorate Adjunct/Part-Time Administrative/Staff Executive (Director, Asst/Assoc VP/Dean) Senior Executive (VP, Dean, President/Chancellor) Please type the characters to the left above (case sensitive). Close Job Seeker Login Email Password Keep me signed in Log In Forgot your password? Don't have an account? Sign Up (New) Terms and Conditions of Use (Updated) Privacy Policy"
