    "https://www.higheredjobs.com/institution/details.cfm?JobCode=179625527&Title=Director%20of%20Student%20Engagement": {
      "title": "Director of Student Engagement",
      "description": "Director of Student Engagement - HigherEdJobs Skip to main content Hide this notification New job search filters and job description pages are here. We'd love your feedback! Share Feedback Sign Up | Log In Log In Sign Up Job Search By Category Administrative Faculty Executive By Location Metro/Region State/Province Country Remote By School Four-Year Institutions Two-Year Institutions All Institutions Institutional Profiles By Type Dual Career Today's Jobs Adjunct/Part-Time Inclusive Workplace Military-Friendly Advanced Search My Account Signed out Account Home Job Alerts Resume/CV Other Documents My Jobs Organizer Profile Account Settings News & Resources News Advice & News Higher Ed Careers Author in Residence Ask the Expert Newsletters HigherEdJobs Podcast Resources Career Resources Job Search Tips Resume/CV Writing Service Workplace Inclusion Search Firms Employers Home Login Create Account Job Postings Post a Single Job Job Packs Unlimited Postings VIP Positions Automated Postings Other Products Digital Advertising Resume Database Institutional Profile Interim Search View All Products Posting Upgrades Inclusive Workplace Upgrade Inclusive Workplace Spotlight Priority Job Upgrade Military Upgrade Social Media Upgrade Featured Executive Position More Info Our Audience Testimonials Pay Your Invoice Contact Us Home Jobs Institution Job Listings Job Detail CU Director of Student Engagement Centenary University Hackettstown, NJ $55,000 - $60,000 per year Apply Now Share this position Copy link Email LinkedIn Facebook X (Twitter) Salary $55,000 - $60,000 per year Job Type Full-Time Category Student Affairs and Services Posted Today Apply By Dec 14, 2026 20 days left Website www.centenaryuniversity.edu Centenary University Mission & Priorities Centenary University launches students into a successful career and life. Centenary advances three strategic priorities: Student Success, University Vitality, and World Engagement. Position Summary The Director of Student Engagement provides leadership for the development, implementation, and assessment of initiatives that enhance student involvement, campus life, student belonging, leadership development, and the overall Centenary student experience. Reporting to the Vice President for Student Affairs, the Director oversees the Campus Activities staff and the First-Year Leaders program, serves as Director of the University's First-Year Experience (FYE) program, and provides strategic direction for student engagement, campus programming, and first-year student transition initiatives. The Director of Student Engagement works collaboratively with faculty, staff, students, and university departments to create meaningful opportunities for students to connect with the University, develop leadership skills, participate in campus life, and build a strong sense of community. Through strategic programming, staff supervision, assessment, and data informed practices, the Director of Student Engagement advances student engagement, satisfaction, persistence, and retention. Core Responsibilities and Expected Outcomes Strategic Leadership, Student Engagement & Belonging Responsibilities - Develop and lead a comprehensive student engagement strategy that strengthens belonging, school spirit, leadership development, and meaningful connections among students, faculty, staff, alumni, and the broader Centenary community. - Partner across the University to create initiatives that enhance student engagement, satisfaction, persistence, and retention while supporting the overall student experience. - Collaborate with Academic Affairs, Athletics, Enrollment Management, Advancement, Communications, and other campus partners to deliver integrated co-curricular experiences that support institutional priorities. - Utilize student feedback, participation data, engagement metrics, and assessment results to evaluate effectiveness and drive continuous improvement of programs and services. - Promote engagement opportunities through effective communication strategies and expand connections between students, alumni, community partners, and other members of the Centenary network. Expected Outcomes - Increase student participation in campus activities, organizations, leadership opportunities, and co-curricular programming while maintaining broad representation across student populations. - Achieve student satisfaction with engagement opportunities and demonstrate year-over-year improvement in students' reported sense of belonging, connection to Centenary, and awareness of campus resources. - Establish and maintain collaborative partnerships across academic and administrative departments, resulting in student engagement initiatives that contribute to achieving institutional goals for student persistence and retention, with annual engagement and retention metrics showing measurable progress. First-Year Experience (FYE) Program Leadership & Oversight Responsibilities - Provide strategic leadership, coordination, implementation, and assessment of the University's First-Year Experience (FYE), ensuring a comprehensive transition experience that supports students' academic, social, and personal success. - Develop and implement programs, initiatives, and support strategies that promote student engagement, belonging, persistence, retention, and successful transition to university life, including identifying and connecting students with appropriate resources and support services. -Collaborate with Academic Affairs, Academic Advising, Student Success, Enrollment Management, Student Affairs, faculty, and other campus partners to create an integrated first-year experience, while overseeing the recruitment, training, development, and assessment of First-Year Leaders and peer mentoring initiatives. - Establish program goals, learning outcomes, and assessment strategies; utilize student engagement, satisfaction, persistence, and retention data to evaluate effectiveness, inform decision-making, and continuously improve the first-year student experience. Expected Outcomes - Deliver a coordinated and impactful First-Year Experience that supports student transition, engagement, belonging, and overall success throughout the first year. - Increase first-year student participation in orientation, campus activities, leadership opportunities, and engagement programs while strengthening connections with peers, faculty, staff, and campus resources. - Recruit, develop, and support a high-performing First-Year Leader program that effectively facilitates new student transition, engagement, and community building. - Improve first-year student satisfaction, persistence, and retention through data-informed assessment, continuous improvement, and responsive programming. Student Retention, Persistence & Early Intervention Support Responsibilities - Partner across the University to develop and implement engagement, retention, and student success strategies that strengthen student connection, belonging, persistence, and completion. - Utilize engagement, participation, satisfaction, and student success data to identify students who may benefit from additional outreach, support, or referrals and coordinate proactive interventions with campus partners. - Lead engagement-focused retention initiatives that connect students with meaningful relationships, campus resources, mentoring opportunities, and co-curricular experiences that support academic and personal success. -Assess the effectiveness of retention and engagement initiatives, using data and student feedback to drive continuous improvement and inform institutional retention strategies. Expected Outcomes - Increase student participation in engagement opportunities, support programs, and initiatives that promote belonging, persistence, and success. - Improve the identification, outreach, and support of students who may be at risk of disengagement or departure through coordinated campus partnerships and referral processes. - Demonstrate measurable improvement in student satisfaction, sense of belonging, and connection to the University. -Contribute to achieving institutional goals for student persistence and retention through data-informed engagement and support strategies. Campus Activities, Student Organizations & Leadership Development Responsibilities - Provide strategic leadership and oversight for campus activities, student organizations, leadership development, and student engagement programming, ensuring alignment with Student Affairs and University priorities. - Foster a vibrant, inclusive campus culture that promotes student involvement, leadership development, school spirit, institutional pride, and a strong sense of belonging. - Collaborate with student leaders, campus partners, alumni, and community stakeholders to enhance programming, strengthen student organizations, and create meaningful opportunities for engagement and leadership. - Utilize assessment, participation data, and student feedback to guide program development, resource allocation, and continuous improvement. Expected Outcomes - Increase student participation in campus events, leadership opportunities, student organizations, and co-curricular experiences. - Achieve student satisfaction with campus engagement opportunities while demonstrating year-over-year improvement in students' sense of belonging and connection to Centenary. - Maintain active and sustainable student organizations with effective leadership transitions and increased student ownership of campus life. - Strengthen campus traditions, school spirit, and institutional pride through high-impact programming, expanded alumni participation, and effective cross-campus collaboration. First-Year Leaders Program Supervision & Development Responsibilities - Provide strategic leadership and oversight of the First-Year Leaders program, including recruitment, training, development, and assessment, to support new student transition, engagement, and success. - Equip First-Year Leaders to serve as effective peer mentors, campus ambassadors, and connectors to university resources, involvement opportunities, and the Centenary community. - Integrate First-Year Leaders into orientation, transition programming, and ongoing first-year engagement initiatives while fostering leadership growth and program sustainability. - Utilize assessment data and stakeholder feedback to evaluate program effectiveness and drive continuous improvement. Expected Outcomes - Recruit, develop, and retain a high-performing First-Year Leader team, with 100% completion of required training and development. - Increase first-year student engagement, resource awareness, and participation in transition and campus involvement opportunities. - Improve first-year student satisfaction, sense of belonging, and connection to the Centenary community. - Maintain a sustainable, assessment-driven First-Year Leaders program that demonstrates measurable contributions to first-year student success and retention. Student Engagement Assessment, Retention & Institutional Collaboration Responsibilities - Lead assessment and continuous improvement efforts by measuring student engagement, belonging, participation, and program effectiveness to inform decision-making and institutional priorities. - Utilize engagement and student success data to identify opportunities for targeted outreach, early intervention, and retention-focused support in partnership with campus stakeholders. - Collaborate across the University to advance student engagement, retention, and success initiatives while leveraging campus, community, and alumni partnerships to enhance the student experience. - Establish departmental goals, performance measures, and strategic recommendations aligned with divisional and institutional priorities. Expected Outcomes - Demonstrate measurable improvement in student engagement, participation, awareness of campus resources, and sense of belonging. - Identify engagement gaps and implement targeted outreach strategies that increase student connection, support utilization, and persistence. - Strengthen cross-functional collaboration and coordination of student success, engagement, and retention initiatives across the University. - Deliver annual assessment results and data-informed recommendations that contribute to institutional goals for student experience, first-year success, and retention. Qualifications Bachelor's degree or equivalent combination of education and  experience required; Master's degree in Higher Education, Student Affairs,  Educational Leadership, Counseling, or a related field preferred. Minimum of five (5) years of progressively responsible experience  in student affairs, student engagement, first-year experience, retention,  or related higher education functions. Demonstrated experience leading student success, engagement,  retention, or leadership development initiatives. Experience supervising staff, student employees, peer leaders, or  student organizations. Strong leadership, communication, collaboration, and project  management skills. Experience using assessment, engagement, and student success data  to drive decision-making and continuous improvement. Ability to work occasional evenings and weekends in support of  university programs and events Centenary University is a learning community comprised of multifaceted and complex differences and we welcome all. We offer a supportive environment that promotes acceptance, a culture of service, skills of critical thought, and purposeful action. We are responsible for the efforts needed to create the change we seek. Equal Employment Opportunity has been, and will continue to be, a fundamental principle at Centenary University where employment is based upon personal capabilities and qualifications without discrimination because of race, color, religion, sex, age, national or ethnic origin, sexual orientation, marital status, service in Armed Forces, disability or any other protected characteristic as established by law. This policy of Equal Employment Opportunity applies to policies and procedures relating to recruitment, hiring, promotion, compensation, benefits, termination and other terms and conditions of employment. Apply Now Share this position Copy link Email LinkedIn Facebook X (Twitter) CU Centenary University 4-Year & Advanced · Hackettstown, NJ At the main campus in Hackettstown, N.J., the equestrian center, and the Parsippany campus, the University enrolls approximately 1,100 undergraduate students and a nearly equal number of adult and graduate... 5 open positions View profile Create your free job search account Edit and manage Job Alerts Post your resume/CV Track your applications Join Now Have an account? Sign in To Apply for this Job Email: Kerry.mullins@centenaryuniversity.edu OR Apply through HigherEdJobs Please be sure to read the job posting carefully and submit all required information. Job Seekers Search Jobs Job Seeker Login Advice & News Newsletter Sign-Up Employers Post A Job All Recruitment Products Employer Login Testimonials Company About Us Contact Us Advertise with Us Our Audience Job Seekers Search Jobs Job Seeker Login Advice & News Newsletter Sign-Up Employers Post A Job All Recruitment Products Employer Login Testimonials Company About Us Contact Us Advertise with Us Our Audience Privacy Policy | Terms of Use | Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information © 2026 HigherEdJobs. U.S. Patent 8,548,928 Email this job to a friend Email Job To Please enter a single email address Your Email Your Name Message Insider Update Sign me up for the Insider Update , HigherEdJobs' newsletter for career-focused higher education professionals. Privacy Policy Insider Career Track: -- Select a Career Track -- Student Faculty Member (Tenured) Faculty Member (Non-Tenured) Post Doctorate Adjunct/Part-Time Administrative/Staff Executive (Director, Asst/Assoc VP/Dean) Senior Executive (VP, Dean, President/Ch